{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"A\":\"Research algorithmic restructuring: profile bubble-sort/mode/variance costs and build a semantics-preserving candidate using faster per-column sorting and a linear mode scan. Preserve the observable calculation/order carefully: input is stored column-major; mean and harmonic sums occur before sorting; variance sums sorted values; output is rounded to one decimal. Establish mode/tie behavior from oracle comparisons rather than the prose, including the source’s uninitialized counter issue. Validate exact output on broad generated valid matrices before proposing it.\",\"B\":\"Research CPU parallelism only: columns are independent, so evaluate OpenMP work-sharing over sufficiently large column workloads, with serial fallback/thresholds to avoid startup and scheduling overhead. Keep all reductions within each column in the original operation order, retain serial formatted output, and avoid unsafe floating-point flags. Measure both small and large valid matrices; the 4-core ARM target and 9.844 ms baseline make overhead a primary risk. Submit an independently correct, measured candidate rather than assuming four threads help.\",\"C\":\"Research low-level single-thread costs: quantify parsing, allocation, sorting, metric passes, and output. Explore conservative improvements such as buffered I/O, fewer allocations/passes, cache-friendly per-column processing, and compiler-safe loop improvements, but do not use lossy numeric parsing, fast-math, or input-specific shortcuts. Any parser must accept the full valid double input domain and candidate output must byte-match the oracle across varied dimensions, values, duplicates, and signs. Report measured net benefit relative to the 9.844 ms baseline.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates with independent correctness evidence and repeatable timing. Benchmark each candidate and each proposed combination against the valid baseline (mean 0.009844 s, three samples, four correctness cases); include cold/startup-sensitive small inputs and larger inputs. Do not presume algorithmic, I/O, and OpenMP gains add. Retain the fastest robust exact-output version, reject regressions/noise-level changes, and ensure compilation/run configuration remains within the supplied target constraints.\",\"analysis\":\"The workload is descriptive statistics over transposed, column-contiguous doubles. Likely opportunities are replacing O(columns*rows^2) bubble sorting, linearizing mode after sorting, reducing passes/I/O, and conditional 4-core column parallelism. Exact observable behavior matters more than intended prose because formatted one-decimal output and floating-point accumulation order can expose changes. The only measurement is a correct 9.844 ms baseline, so fixed process/thread overhead may dominate and every integration requires direct measurement.\"}"}}
